  "answer": "### Short Answer\nIf you have missed the deadline for filing your annual income tax return, you may be subject to penalties and interest on the unpaid tax. It is advisable to file your return as soon as possible to minimize these penalties.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51 of the NIRC specifies that individuals are required to file their income tax returns on or before the fifteenth day of April each year. If this deadline is missed, the taxpayer may incur penalties as stipulated in Section 72, which includes a fine and interest on the unpaid tax amount.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nPractically, if you have missed the deadline, you should file your return immediately to avoid further penalties. The longer you wait, the more penalties and interest may accrue. It is also important to ensure that any tax due is paid to avoid additional charges. If you are unable to pay the full amount, consider discussing payment options with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
